  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rhino &amp; Tiger Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to (1) facilitate routine field patrols in KSNP and adjoining buffer zone forests; (2) perform targeted forest patrols to reduce seasonal poaching; (3) maintain forest-edge community relationships so that information will be provided relevant to suspected crime sites; (4) support law enforcement efforts by confirming and responding to species or forest crime; (5) maintain and develop strong relationships between Tiger Protection and Conservation Unit personnel and forest-edge farmers; (6) provide support to local NGOs; (8) enforce species and habitat protection law directly within park jurisdictions or in partnership with other agencies outside the park; (9) work with local NGOs and government agencies on tiger issues; (10) provide relevant agencies with patrol data on developing threats to tiger habitat; (11) respond to wildlife emergencies; (12) carry out routine awareness activities; (13) provide information to local NGO partners and district governments on key tiger habitats; (14) involve the National Park Authority staff in program activities; (16) identify funding and opportunities for NPA ranger and manager training: and (17) provide technical support to secure pilot implementation of Law 48 on human tiger conflict mitigation in a pilot area adjoining the national park.</narrative>
  </description>
